This project analyzes cardiovascular health data to explore factors associated with heart attack risk.

# Data
  (https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/fatemehmohammadinia/heart-attack-dataset-tarik-a-rashid)

**Variables:**

- `Age`: Patient age in years (Numeric Discrete)
- `Gender`: 1 = Male 0 = Female (categorical)
- `Heart.Rate`: Heart beats per minute (Numeric Discrete)
- `Systolic.blood.pressure`: Max BP (mm Hg) (Numeric Discrete)
- `Diastolic.blood.pressure`: Min BP (mm Hg) (Numeric Discrete)
- `Blood Sugar`: Blood Sugar level (Numeric Discrete)
- `CK-MB`: Enzyme level indicating muscle damage (Numeric Continuous)
- `Troponin`: Cardiac biomarker (Numeric Continuous)
- `Result`: positive = Had heart attack 0 = No heart attack (Categorical)
---

# Question 

> Is there a difference in Age between patients who had heart attacks and those who did not?

> Can we predict Troponin levels using CK-MB and Systolic Blood Pressure?
---  


### Load libraries and Data
```{r}
library(tidyverse)

heart_attack <- read.csv('./heartAttack.csv')
```


# Descriptive Analysis

## Histogram: Blood Sugar Distribution
```{r}
heart_attack |>
  ggplot(aes(x = Blood.sugar)) +
  geom_histogram(fill = "steelblue", color = "black") +
  labs(title = "Age Distribution")

```

## BoxPlot: Troponin levels by Result
```{r}
heart_attack |>
  ggplot(aes(x = Result, y = Age)) +
  geom_boxplot(fill = "lightcoral") +
  labs(x = "Heart Attack", title = "Troponin Levels by Heart Attack Result")

```
## Summary of the data
```{r}
heart_attack |>
  filter(Heart.rate != 1111) |>
  group_by(Result) |>
  summarize(mean_heartrate = mean(Heart.rate, na.rm = TRUE),
            sd_heartrate = sd(Heart.rate, na.rm = TRUE),
            min_heartrate = min(Heart.rate, na.rm = TRUE),
            max_heartrate = max(Heart.rate, na.rm = TRUE))

```
